# One holding for every entry of the Kodeks Dyplomatyczny Wielkopolski the
# edition uses, whatever its volume (the editor, 2026-10-16: "They should be
# presented as a single unit on the site ... Each entry should be treated as
# its own document"). A printed edition, read in the Wielkopolska Digital
# Library's electronic text of each volume; there are no page images (the
# editor: text only).

slug: kdw
# The site prints the library's short name before it: "BK PAN Kodeks
# Dyplomatyczny Wielkopolski". Each document's own place in the Kodeks
# (volume, number) is in rulings.yml, `documents: citation:`, and is shown on
# its page.
ref: "Kodeks Dyplomatyczny Wielkopolski"
archive: PAN Biblioteka Kórnicka (BK PAN)
title: >-
  Medieval documents on Trąbczyn and its neighbourhood printed in the Kodeks
  Dyplomatyczny Wielkopolski, the edition of the charters of Greater Poland
  to 1444, each entry with its editors' heading, summary, sources and notes.
title_de: >-
  Mittelalterliche Urkunden über Trąbczyn und seine Umgebung aus dem Kodeks
  Dyplomatyczny Wielkopolski, der Edition der großpolnischen Urkunden bis
  1444, jeder Eintrag mit Überschrift, Regest, Quellen und Anmerkungen seiner
  Herausgeber.
archive_title: >-
  Kodeks Dyplomatyczny Wielkopolski (Codex diplomaticus Maioris Poloniae)
date_span: "984-1444"
status: draft              # draft | transcribed | translated | published
published_tag: ""

# The era of the Middle Ages, a working name until the editor names it
# (the editor, 2026-10-16: a new era).
era: medieval

repository: bkpan-kornik

# The source of the text: the WBC's electronic text of each volume
# (intake/kdw_source.py, VOLUMES, has the eight links). Saved in raw_dir.
scan_source: Wielkopolska Biblioteka Cyfrowa, electronic text of each volume (https://www.wbc.poznan.pl/)

scans:
  raw_dir: J:/Documents/Archive/Genealogy/References/Kodeks Dyplomatyczny Wielkopolski
  raw_glob: "*.jpg"
  ascii_prefix: BKPAN_KDW

transcriptions:
  dir: transcriptions
  glob: "*.txt"
  page_id_strip: ""

corpus: corpus.txt

description: >-
  Entries of the Kodeks Dyplomatyczny Wielkopolski (Codex diplomaticus
  Maioris Poloniae), the edition of the medieval documents of Greater
  Poland to 1444, published at Poznań in eleven volumes from 1877 to 1999:
  volumes 1 to 4 (1877-1881) and 5 (1908) for the Poznań Society of Friends
  of Learning, 6 to 11 (1982-1999) in its series of source editions. Each
  document of this holding is one entry, given whole: the entry's number,
  the editors' heading (place and date), their summary of the document (in
  Latin in volumes 1 to 5, in Polish in 6 to 11), the list of manuscripts
  and earlier editions, the text of the document (Latin, at times Polish or
  German), and the editors' notes and identifications of places. Some
  entries of volume 5 are a summary only. The entries come from the
  electronic text of each volume in the Wielkopolska Digital Library, from
  the copies of the Kórnik Library of the Polish Academy of Sciences.

translation_note: >-
  An entry of a printed edition: the first lines are the modern editors'
  (heading, summary, sources), then the medieval text, then their notes. The
  editors' summary is Latin in volumes 1 to 5 and Polish in 6 to 11; the
  sources use their abbreviations (Or. original, Kop. copy, Wyd. edition,
  Reg. regest). "^1" is a footnote mark; "[s. 443]" is the page of the
  manuscript the editors printed from. Names of places are given as the
  document writes them, and the notes say what place the editors take them
  to be.
